{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Property","symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"dashLength"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","text":"MXLTenths"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"title":"dashLength","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLWedgeV10dashLengthSdSgvp","role":"symbol"},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlwedge\/dashlength"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"dashLength"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTenths","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","text":"MXLTenths"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dash-length"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLWedge\/dashLength","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLWedge"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The length, in tenths, of the dashes in a dashed line. Ignored if the corresponding line-type attribute is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not dashed."}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTenths":{"abstract":[{"text":"The tenths type is a number representing tenths of interline staff space (positive or negative). Both integer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and decimal values are allowed, such as 5 for a half space and 2.5 for a quarter space. Interline space is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"measured from the middle of a staff line.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLTenths","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTenths"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTenths"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltenths","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTenths"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLWedge":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLWedge","title":"MXLWedge","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLWedge","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLWedge","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlwedge","abstract":[{"text":"The wedge type represents crescendo and diminuendo wedge symbols. The type attribute is crescendo for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"start of a wedge that is closed at the left side, and diminuendo for the start of a wedge that is closed on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the right side. Spread values are measured in tenths; those at the start of a crescendo wedge or end of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"diminuendo wedge are ignored. The niente attribute is yes if a circle appears at the point of the wedge,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indicating a crescendo from nothing or diminuendo to nothing. It is no by default, and used only when the type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is crescendo, or the type is stop for a wedge that began with a diminuendo type. The line-type is solid if not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specified.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLWedge/dashLength":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlwedge\/dashlength","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLWedge\/dashLength","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dashLength","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTenths","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"title":"dashLength","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The length, in tenths, of the dashes in a dashed line. Ignored if the corresponding line-type attribute is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not dashed."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol"}}}